INT. STALLED CABLE CAR GONDOLA - DAY

RAVI, forties, a hiking guide, sits on the floor with his boots braced against the door. NKECHI, thirties, grips the rail. OLEG, seventies, holds a thermos in both hands. PILAR, twenties, films the white nothing outside on her phone.

The gondola has been still for two hours. He licks his lips. She lowers the phone. They all look at the roof as it ticks in the cold.

RAVI
Rescue said four hours. That was one hour ago, so three.

NKECHI
It was two hours ago. So two.

OLEG
It is whatever number keeps us calm. I choose three.

PILAR
My battery is nineteen percent.

RAVI
Then stop filming the clouds.

PILAR
They're getting closer.

NKECHI
Clouds don't get closer. We get lower.

OLEG
Nobody said lower.

RAVI
The cable sags in the cold. It is normal. Everybody breathe slowly, in through the nose.

PILAR
I am breathing. I'm breathing so loudly.

NKECHI
We are fine. Somebody pour the tea.

OLEG
Last cup is mine. After that, we take turns.
